  "hints": [
    "Set `decoder.dateDecodingStrategy` before decoding.",
    "Use `.iso8601`, `.secondsSince1970`, `.millisecondsSince1970` or `.formatted(dateFormatter)`.",
    "Render with `date.ISO8601Format()`."
  ],
  "impact": "core",
  "jsBridge": "`dateDecodingStrategy` (`.iso8601`, `.secondsSince1970`, custom) tells `JSONDecoder` how dates look in JSON. JS `JSON.parse` leaves dates as strings, and revivers are manual.",
  "compass": [
    {
      "kind": "js",
      "q": "JS: `JSON.parse(text, (k, v) => k === 'at' ? new Date(v) : v)`. What does a decoding strategy centralise?"
    },
    {
      "kind": "edge",
      "q": "ISO strings with fractional seconds: does `.iso8601` accept them? What's the fix?"
    },
    {
      "kind": "contrast",
      "q": "Global strategy on the decoder vs a custom `init(from:)` per type: when is each right?"
    },
    {
      "kind": "practice",
      "q": "Backend sends milliseconds, not seconds. What bug do you see if you pick `.secondsSince1970`?"
    }
  ],
